WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.600
The Centro Sea stretches across
the southern region of Rumeliana.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.110
Located in a key position
that divides the Centro east and west

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:10.280
is the port city-state of Phoinike.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:15.410
It was the capital of the ancient
ocean empire Phoinike

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.950
that ruled the Centro for over 1800 years.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.290
Standing on the southern tip
is the Greater Lighthouse,

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.750
which still harbors traces of its ancient past.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.890
That's a Balt-Rhein Imperial ship.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.220
Oh, we're finally here.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.780
The crystal cliff carved by man.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.700
It protects the city from invaders,

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:05.420
and the ore mined from it is their greatest export.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.540
This Pyramis was also made from Phoiniken crystal.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.590
I should first find the kulak.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.680
Do not turn around.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.690
Please, pretend that I am not talking to you.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:31.230
It is nice to make your acquaintance, Mahmut Bey.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.110
I am the kulak Kiros.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.410
This is your first time in Phoinike, yes?

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:39.240
-Yes.
-However...

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:42.330
Before you even set foot on the ship
that brought you here,

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:47.370
the members of the Phoiniken senate
were fully aware of your movements.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.670
You have come at a bad time.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.880
Trouble will almost certainly find you here.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.510
You must have seen the Imperial envoy
that arrived just before you?

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.760
Hey, you know, I haven't had lunch yet.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:01.430
Would you like to join me?

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.010
Oh, sounds good.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.890
There aren't a lot of customers today.
Might as well take a break.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.650
You are Mahmut Pasha?

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:11.940
Yes.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.190
We are here to welcome you.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.450
Phoinike's Magistros Lord Konstantinos

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.530
is awaiting you.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.410
The City of the Lighthouse

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:45.220
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.270
An Imperial uniform...

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.770
That must be the envoy.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.860
Torqye garb and a golden eagle.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.120
Please, forgive my insolence.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.910
I am the Magistros Konstantinos.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.620
I was just very eager to meet you.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.830
There is not a soul in Phoinike
who does not know your name

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.630
Tughril Mahmut Pasha.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.880
We are about to conduct an emergency assembly,

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.470
and I would like you to join us.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.720
Me?

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.390
Just now, an Imperial envoy

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:52.730
requested we cede a section of our port
for the Empire to use for their fleet.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.230
We were given ten days for a response.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.230
This is not an issue that only concerns our nation.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.190
Two months ago,

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:05.820
an Imperial fleet entered the Tharros Harbor
located to the south of Phoinike,

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.950
on a so-called visit to the Tharros King,

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.120
where they still remain today.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:16.170
Tharros is an independent city-state,
rich in agriculture.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:21.170
Five years ago, the Empire approached Tharros
to present them with a trade agreement.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.420
Five years ago?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.260
That is the year Minister Louis came into power.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.760
In the last two months-- No, since five years ago,

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:30.850
the 12 city-states of Centro

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:36.270
have been fearing when and whom
the Empire will strike from Tharros.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:41.730
But I would actually welcome the Empire
to attack Phoinike.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:43.940
If they do,

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.740
then we, the descendents of the great ancient empire,

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.320
would be able to teach them
the true meaning of empire.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:54.870
An empire should honor the values of
the many nations under its rule,

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.910
protect their lives and livelihoods,

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.170
and work towards mutual prosperity together.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:04.460
Balt-Rhein who only knows how to control
other nations through their military might,

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.840
has no right to call themselves an empire.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.720
You will join us, won't you?

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:15.890
We only have to cede a section of our port.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:20.650
That small price will allow us to live as we have.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.770
A cession only in name.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:25.530
This is an invasion.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:27.900
We are the descendents of the true empire.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.780
How could we bend
to such an imitation of an empire?

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.910
Refusing their request means war.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:40.500
Kaisaras, you should consider the reason
the Empire would target Phoinike.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:45.170
Phoinike is a key location that resides
at the center of the Centro.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:49.090
If they controlled it, they could rule the Centro.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.510
Yes, control the Centro.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.720
That is what Minister Louis aims to do.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.520
And if this area fell to the Empire,

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.640
Torqye would be surrounded on three sides.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:04.230
However, Phoinike has the Great Lighthouse
built by our founder, Emperor Phoenix.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.730
As well as the Great Wall.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:10.740
It has held back invaders for 3000 years,
since our nation's founding.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:14.910
We should reject these demands,
and make preparations for war immediately.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.620
You fool. You're blinding yourself with our past glory.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:23.670
No nation has ever defeated the Balt-Rhein Empire
in the last 400 years.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.920
Because nobody thought to try.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:28.710
However, it was Mahmut Pasha there

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:32.260
who showed the world
it was not impossible in Hisar.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:34.930
Is that truly the Mahmut Pasha?

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.100
That there?

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:38.680
Is this the reason I was brought here?

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:42.770
He claimed victory over the Empire's forces
all on his own.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.110
Please, stop.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:46.320
Not only am I no longer Pasha,

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.190
it is not as though I fought their army in Hisar.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:53.700
Everything I did in Hisar
was to avoid all-out war with the Empire.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:55.910
Oh, a truly humble hero.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.950
You do not wish to be boastful
of your accomplishments.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.750
-No.
-I know.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:04.710
We should have Mahmut Pasha join our discussion.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:09.920
Then it would appear that we are receiving
the support of the Torqye Stratocracy.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.930
Yes, even if we cede the port to the Empire,

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.550
we will have more leverage.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.720
Kaisaras. If we do not fight here,

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:22.350
we will be scorned by the nations
of Centro, nay, the world.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.600
What of it?

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.980
If there is war, our families and friends

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:32.070
and even your beloved city
will all be killed and destroyed.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.700
It's better than abandoning our pride.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:39.040
Kaisaras. Perhaps you are more concerned
about losing your mansion and wealth?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.830
Quiet, everyone.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.040
In accordance with the ancient Phoiniken tradition,

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:50.800
I wish to submit this matter to a vote.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.930
Magistros, do you seriously
wish to fight the Empire?

00:08:56.090 --> 00:09:00.390
Our impregnable nation has a powerful ally.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.890
The Centro's greatest naval fleet,
the Venedik Armada.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:08.690
Venedik and our nation first
forged our alliance over 200 years ago.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:13.530
The Balt-Rhein Empire instituted
their navy only five years ago.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:16.030
They are mere amateurs of naval warfare.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.030
They will be no match for the Venedik Armada.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.620
But... Is there no way to avoid war?

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:27.120
If we claim victory here, it will greatly change
the course of Rumeliana's history.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:30.670
Isn't that right, Mahmut Bey?

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.060
What was the result of the vote?

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:48.230
Which side won?

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.560
Obviously we're not giving in to such demands.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:58.030
The Magistros is returning.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.030
It seems that trouble did find you, just as I predicted.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.080
-Kiros?
-Yes.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.960
I address the nation.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:16.300
In light of the Balt-Rhein Empire's
aggressions against our nation,

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:18.630
Phoinike will take up arms to defend ourselves.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:24.430
We are the descendents of the great Phoiniken Empire
with over 3000 years of history.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:28.270
The Balt-Rhein Empire only has a history of 500 years.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.350
They are nothing more than savages...

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:34.190
There are this many proud descendents
of the ancient empire?

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:38.200
Willing to spill their blood for honor and glory?

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.860
This is a righteous war.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.370
Mahmut Bey.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.080
If you are planning on leaving, now is the time.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:48.620
No, I will stay here.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.170
I cannot stop this anymore.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:56.630
War is about to begin right in front of me.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:11:00.680
And I am unable to do anything.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.770
Engine room, close the harbor.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:15.860
That was a quicker response than I expected.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:18.030
Clinging to past glory,

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.860
they chose their pride.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:33.330
A thousand years ago,
our ancestors worked together

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:37.960
to bring prosperity to the Centro.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:42.890
It has been 300 years since the
Kingdom of Law was absorbed into the Empire.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:47.350
I had hoped we would not have
to betray our old allies.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:54.900
Are you okay?

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:58.440
Is this your first time out to sea, duchess?

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.530
You may be quite daring
on the battlefield, but out at sea...

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:08.240
I just got sick from having to hear you
talk about your lame history.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:15.130
It has been 15 days since the
Balt-Rhein Empire's naval fleet arrived

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:17.290
and laid siege to Phoinike.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.840
Don't stop.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.050
Victory is ours once we make it over.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:22.760
Archers, ready.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:24.300
Fire.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.390
We can't break through. Retreat.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.900
Deserters...

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.780
...shall be shot to death.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:51.620
The Empire's advance guard

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:55.830
were made up of soldiers from the former kingdoms
in the Balt and Rhein regions

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.090
who were absorbed into the Empire.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:01.590
This is how the Empire operates.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.030
While there are so many bodies floating in the sea,

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:24.110
how can it be so peaceful in the city?

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:27.320
Why don't you let me do that for you?

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:28.780
Magistros.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.330
Magistros.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.620
Magistros. You were right.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.000
The Imperials can't make it over the wall.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:40.290
Yes, everyone is doing a great job
keeping them at bay.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:44.210
They could attack a thousand times,
and this nation will never fall.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:46.180
It is true.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:49.850
The Great Wall has been impregnable.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:51.010
However...

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:54.140
Soon our ally Venedik will come.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:59.650
While I know this siege is hard on everyone,
it won't be long now.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:01.980
It's been 15 days since the siege began.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:04.820
I still haven't been able to do anything.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:08.320
I am an outsider here and no longer Pasha.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:11.580
Is there really something I can do here?

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:17.120
The enemy sure is persistent.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.420
Yes, they've already attacked four times today.

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:23.420
Even though we haven't
let a single soldier in the city.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.670
But do you not think it is taking too long?

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:30.140
It is only a nine-day voyage from Venedik.

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:33.680
We signaled for reinforcements 15 days ago.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:35.220
What are you trying to say?

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:37.270
I do not wish to think it,

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:41.900
but maybe Venedik means to betray us
out of fear of the Empire.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:43.570
Nikephoros.

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.820
I'm sorry. I do not know what I was thinking.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:49.150
No, but if that is actually the case,
that is a serious issue.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:52.830
We don't know how long our provisions will last
if the siege continues.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:58.830
This nation cannot win
without Venedik's reinforcements.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:03.090
But prolonging the siege will also
put a strain on our enemy.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:07.380
This is a large undertaking for the Empire as well.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:11.430
In that case, this is a test of endurance
between us and the Empire.

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:15.220
There is only one thing I can do.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:17.720
What is it, Mahmut Bey?

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:22.230
A ship should be sent to Venedik
to bring back the reinforcements directly.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.400
By breaking through the Empire's blockade?

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:28.110
Yes. If you provide me with a ship,

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.200
I will be happy to take on the mission.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:34.070
You?

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:37.410
If they say they will not provide reinforcements,

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.040
I will negotiate.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:41.330
There is no need to take such a risk.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:44.750
-The Venedik Armada will come.
-But they--

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.920
Venedik's Doge Lucio is a personal friend of mine.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:53.640
He is not the kind of man who would break an oath.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:58.180
Ibrahim Vali would never start an uprising!

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.480
Are you unable to see the situation?

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:04.810
I appreciate your sentiments,

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.730
but this matter is closed.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.860
I am sure that the Empire's Minister Louis

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:18.240
has already made moves
to break this stalemate somehow.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:30.800
Looks like only half of us made it to land.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.800
Curse that Louis, and his ridiculous plan.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:38.060
Well, this is better than the choppy sea at least.

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:41.140
For 3000 years, these cliffs have been impregnable.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:42.940
I don't care how many men we lose,

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:46.020
we're going to be the first to break through.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:53.860
Kiros?

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.160
Hey, there.

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:57.740
There's nothing you can say to them.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:02.120
The people in charge of this country
know how to protect themselves.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:06.120
My old man turned into a meek cat
after he lost the vote.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:09.880
-Old man?
-The Kaisaras Apollodorus.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:12.710
Why did a son of a Kaisaras become a kulak?

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.510
My old man's the reason I became a kulak.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.850
My old man, the current Kaisaras,

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:22.390
is a man walled off in his seat of power,

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:25.020
just like this city-state itself.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.690
He'll flatter and lie to anyone

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:30.860
for his own gain and self-preservation,

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:33.030
and bribery was a daily norm.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.990
And everyone around him started to look the same.

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:39.740
I thought that if I stayed there,
I'd end up becoming just like them.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:45.290
Ever since I started thinking that way,
I stopped going back to that household.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:49.590
But no matter how much I wandered
around the city, I didn't find anything.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:54.510
Still, I never tried to leave this place,
just wasting my time.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.180
It was right around that time

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:01.560
that Suleyman Bey was caught inside our mansion.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:06.390
He did a remarkable job infiltrating us,
disguised as a falconer.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.020
Just look at you.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:11.270
So you were rummaging through our papers?

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.730
What were you looking for?

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:18.570
I don't know who you work for,
but you're heading straight to the gallows.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:20.160
Hold on, kid.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:23.450
What are you looking for?

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:28.120
I think you're looking for the same thing I am.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:32.630
I was able to find what I was looking for
because of this job.

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:36.920
I had the feeling a while ago
when I first started watching you.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.550
You and I are the same.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:40.930
Come to my side.

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:45.680
Would you put your life in my hands?

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:53.320
So, Mahmut Bey...

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:56.230
What are you planning to do now?

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:02.570
Part of a kulak's job is
to ensure the safety of other agents.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:06.830
I'd actually like to lead you away
from this battleground as soon as possible.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:11.250
Please, I wish to go secure the reinforcements
from the Venedik Armada.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:16.590
In order to do that, I would appreciate it
if you could provide me a ship and a crew.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:19.930
You heard what I said, didn't you?

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:22.970
Besides, what are you planning on doing
with just one ship?

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:26.680
There are enemy ships surrounding the bay.

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:30.640
Phoinike cannot win without Venedik's help.

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:34.650
In any case, none of this has to do with Torqye.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:38.440
Why are you so desperate to help us?

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.280
Why?

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:45.080
A war started right in front of me,

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:47.450
on my very first visit to this nation.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:51.290
My arrival triggered this war.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:54.960
It would not be fair if I were the only one
to escape this situation.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:59.460
I would like to end this war as soon as possible.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:03.680
Oh, my lamp went out.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:07.350
-Let me help you.
-Oh, be careful, Mahmut Bey.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:10.930
The ground is very unstable here.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:20.400
I'm sorry.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.450
Let's continue our discussion, then.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:29.330
What you're saying is really all for Torqye, isn't it?

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.500
If Phoinike falls to the Empire,

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:35.670
it will give them a good foothold to invade Torqye.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:38.750
So basically, in order to
ensure your own nation's safety,

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:43.720
Phoinike cannot be allowed to lose to the Empire,
no matter the price they may have to pay.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.720
Tell me if I'm wrong.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:51.310
How should I answer him?

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:55.020
What would Suleyman Bey do?

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:56.900
What would Zaganos Pasha do?

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:58.900
Or Halil Pasha?

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:00.940
No.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:04.320
This is between me and him.

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.740
If he lets go, then I will have to accept it.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:10.950
It just means that I could not fulfill my wishes.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:13.710
It is just as you say.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.040
I am a Torqye soldier.

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:18.710
I will prioritize Torqye's safety above all else.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:22.670
I cannot allow the Empire
to gain control of the Centro.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:25.260
If you find that detestable,

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:28.680
then you may let go of my arm.

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:32.430
I just wish to do what I can.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:34.140
Please.

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:36.140
I am asking you

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:40.440
to put your life and your countrymen's in my hands.

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:45.700
Very well.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:48.370
I, Kiros, kulak of the Torqye spy network,

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:50.450
shall lend you my assistance.

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:56.830
Look at you. You've inspired me
to action, Mahmut Bey.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:01.670
This is what I've always been looking for.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:05.510
Something I could stake my life on.

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:08.890
Come to the harbor tomorrow at the break of dawn.

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:13.470
I will arrange a ship and a crew
that can break through the Empire's blockade.

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:16.060
Okay.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:50.650
Every moment, our situation changes.

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:55.280
All I can do now is stop
the Empire's fleet in front of me.

00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:57.290
Next episode, "The Iron Chains."

00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:01.460
At that moment, a gust of wind blows over us.
